<title>CANADA: Imperial Oil raises Canada oil prices.</title>
<headline>Imperial Oil raises Canada oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Oil Ltd said it raised the price it would pay for Edmonton light sweet crude oil by C$5.00/cubic metre or C$0.79/barrel, to C$193.00/cubic metre or C$30.68/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Other new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$186.00/cubic metre, or C$29.57/barrel</p>
<p>Bow River at Hardisty C$153.00/cubic metre, or C$24.33/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$161.00/cubic metre, or C$25.60/barrel</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
